---
description: Triage PokeFarm failures with a compact precomputed packet; expand context only when the one-id debugger cannot establish the defect.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow @.claude/skills/pokefarm-triage/SKILL.md.

For interactive queue work, select one group with `pokepilot_get_triage()`,
then run `make -s debug RUN=<representative-run-id>`. For unattended work the
shell already selected the group and normally attaches a **Prepared debug
packet**; consume it directly and do not pick another failure.

Start from the packet's deterministic replay and `source_matches`, fix the
shared invariant, rerun the same one-id debug command, then `make test-short`.
Only expand to full run debug, recovery audit, or a named artifact when the
compact packet leaves a specific ambiguity. Raw recordings and broad repository
search are last-resort evidence.
